GEN Notes for Interview

- This project uses Playwright to automate web testing.
- Tests are organized in the `tests` folder for browser and API checks.
- Page Object Model is used in `PageObject` folder to keep selectors and actions separate.
- Login flow and inventory flow are separated into reusable page files.
- API tests are in `tests/APITest` to validate endpoints and responses.
- Test data and environment settings are stored in `Testdata` and `config` folders.
- The project runs tests with Playwright config and generates a report in `playwright-report`.
- `allure-results` is used to collect test report data.
- Simple JavaScript helper files are used for reusable utilities.
- Good to mention both UI and API testing skills in interview.
- Focus on strong test structure, maintainability, and easy debugging.
- Explain how automation saves time and reduces manual testing errors.
